WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.270
The district wants the average science

2
00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:04.750
mark for every class, every term.

3
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.460
That used to be my whole

4
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.940
Saturday, with a calculator.

5
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.440
Now it's one query.

6
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.340
Today: counts and averages for

7
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.380
every group, with GROUP BY.

8
00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.370
SQL can summarise as well as list.

9
00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.390
COUNT counts rows.

10
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.780
AVG gives the average, and MIN and

11
00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.600
MAX the lowest and highest.

12
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.930
And ROUND tidies the decimals.

13
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.360
On their own, they summarise the

14
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.960
whole table into one row.

15
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.580
GROUP BY splits the rows into groups, one

16
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.120
per class, and summarises each group.

17
00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.410
So you get one row for every class.

18
00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.230
A group is all the rows that share a

19
00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.890
value, like every row for Six B.

20
00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.720
Every column you select must be

21
00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.360
grouped, or summarised.

22
00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:02.330
WHERE filters rows before they're grouped.

23
00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.890
HAVING filters the groups after:

24
00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.790
HAVING a count above thirty keeps

25
00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:08.950
only the big classes.

26
00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:10.860
Quick check!

27
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:14.390
Musa missed the science test, so

28
00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:16.670
his mark is empty: NULL.

29
00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:19.870
When I average the marks, what

30
00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.330
does AVG do with his?

31
00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:27.100
AVG skips it: Musa's empty mark is

32
00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.040
left out, not counted as zero.

33
00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.720
Counting the mark column skips it too,

34
00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:34.660
but COUNT star counts every row.

35
00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.410
So when the two counts differ,

36
00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:38.930
something is missing.

37
00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.990
Summaries hide glitches.

38
00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.300
Before you trust an average, ask for the

39
00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.560
lowest and highest in each group.

40
00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.400
A science mark of ninety-nine out

41
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.000
of twenty jumps out at once.

42
00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.680
In the app, a week of hourly soil

43
00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.160
readings becomes one average per

44
00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.540
day: that's a GROUP BY day.

45
00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:03.390
Leave out the glitches, and watch days

46
00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:06.390
four and five rise by about three

47
00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.250
while the median doesn't move.

48
00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:09.990
Your turn.

49
00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.460
After grouping by class, I want only the

50
00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:15.380
classes with more than thirty pupils.

51
00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.250
Which line does that?

52
00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.110
HAVING, because it filters

53
00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:21.450
groups after they're counted.

54
00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.800
Remember: COUNT, AVG, MIN

55
00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.040
and MAX summarise.

56
00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:31.110
GROUP BY makes one row per group.

57
00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.580
And NULLs are skipped, so check the lowest

58
00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:36.640
and highest before you trust an average.

59
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.240
Try it in class tomorrow: pupils

60
00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.960
group themselves by birth month.

61
00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.040
Each group counts itself, and the class

62
00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.280
writes one row per month on the board.

63
00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.060
That's GROUP BY, done with people.
